# distcc — real-world examples

## Install and configure

```sh
# Edit /etc/default/distcc and set:
#   STARTDISTCC="true"
#   ALLOWEDNETS="127.0.0.1 192.168.1.0/24"   # your machine + LAN
#   #LISTENER="127.0.0.1"                    # comment out to listen on LAN
#   ZEROCONF="true"                          # auto discovery

# Install distcc on EVERY machine in the pool.
# Only the main host needs the libraries/headers.

# Start/restart the daemon on each server before compiling
sudo systemctl restart distccd
```

## Compile with auto-discovered hosts (zeroconf)

```sh
# 4 parallel jobs across the network; for C use CC='distcc gcc'
ZEROCONF='+zeroconf' make -j4 CXX='distcc g++'
```

## Compile with a static host list

```sh
DISTCC_HOSTS='127.0.0.1 192.168.1.69' make -j4 CXX='distcc g++'
```

## Show available hosts

```sh
ZEROCONF='+zeroconf' distcc --show-hosts
```

## Homelab: spread a kernel build across homelab and mediaserver

```sh
DISTCC_HOSTS='localhost homelab mediaserver' make -j8 CC='distcc gcc'
```

## Monitor jobs in real time

```sh
distccmon-text 1
```
